/-!
# Descending a second blowup centre to the base, chart by chart

Let `R` be a ring, `I ⊆ R` an ideal and `a : ι → R` a finite family of elements of `I`. The
blowup of `Spec R` in `I` is covered by the charts `Spec R[I/a j]`, on each of which the inverse
image of `I` is the principal ideal generated by the image of `a j`, and every element is a
fraction `x / a j ^ n` with `x ∈ I ^ n`. A closed subscheme of the blowup is given by an ideal
`K j` on each chart.

This file carries out, in pure commutative algebra, the construction of Stacks Lemma 31.32.5
([Stacks, Tag 0803]) for that situation: it produces one ideal `J ⊆ I ^ d` of the **base**, of
finite type, whose extension to each chart is `(I · R[I/a j]) ^ d · K j`. That is the ideal the
composition theorem for admissible blowups, `Stacks.Blowup.IsAdmissibleBlowup.comp`
([Stacks, Tag 080L]), needs, read on the charts of [Stacks, Tag 0804]. The scheme-level
assembly is `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/SecondCentreChart.lean` and
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/SecondCentreFactorization.lean`.

The construction is the one the source indicates: write each generator of `K j` as a fraction
`x / a j ^ n`, and take `J` to be generated by the numerators `a i ^ (d - n) · x` for `d` large.
The only thing "`d` large" has to beat is the clearing of denominators between two charts, and
that is isolated here as the hypothesis `clear`: a fraction lying in `K i` lands, after
multiplication by a sufficiently high power of `a i`, in `K j` as well. On the charts of a
blowup `clear` is the statement that the `K j` are the restrictions of a single quasi-coherent
ideal sheaf, read over the overlap of the two charts.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_fg_le_pow_map_eq_pow_mul`: the ideal `J`, its degree `d`, and the two
  properties `J ≤ I ^ d` and `J · B j = (I · B j) ^ d · K j`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_pow_mul_mem_of_algebraMap_mem_map` and
  `Stacks.Blowup.pow_mul_eq_map_of_pow_mul_eq`: the two steps that turn the membership
  statement a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf gives over the overlap of two charts -- membership
  after inverting the transition element -- into the hypothesis `clear` above.

## Implementation notes

Nothing is assumed about the charts beyond what the affine blowup algebras satisfy, and the
charts are abstracted as an arbitrary family of rings `B j` with ring maps `φ j : R ⟶ B j`.
What is used is

* `princ`, that `I` extends to the principal ideal generated by the image of `a j` — for the
  affine blowup algebra this is Stacks tag 07Z3 (2),
  `Stacks.Blowup.affineBlowup_idealMap_eq_span`;
* `num`, that each chosen generator `z j l` of `K j` is a fraction with numerator in a power of
  `I`, in the denominator-free form `φ j (a j) ^ n j l * z j l = φ j (x j l)` — for the affine
  blowup algebra this is the description by representatives,
  `Stacks.Blowup.affineBlowup_mem_iff`, applied to a finite generating set of `K j`;
* `clear`, the overlap condition described above, again denominator-free.

No nonzerodivisor hypothesis is needed, and it is not assumed that the `a j` generate `I`: the
charts enter only through those three conditions, so the statement applies verbatim to a
subfamily and to any other presentation of the charts. In particular the degree `d` is produced,
not prescribed, and only an upper bound for the exponents is used, so enlarging `d` is harmless.

Degrees are split with `Nat.exists_eq_add_of_le`; truncated subtraction appears only in the
exponent `d - n i l` of the generators of `J`, where `Nat.sub_add_cancel` and `omega` recover
the additive form.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0803](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0803)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 080L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/080L)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0804](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0804)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07Z3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07Z3)
-/

@[expose] public section

open Pointwise

universe u v w

namespace Stacks.Blowup

/-- If `a ∈ I` and `x ∈ I ^ n` with `n ≤ d`, then `a ^ (d - n) * x ∈ I ^ d`. -/
theorem pow_sub_mul_mem_pow {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {I : Ideal R} {a x : R} {n d : ℕ}
    (ha : a ∈ I) (hx : x ∈ I ^ n) (hnd : n ≤ d) : a ^ (d - n) * x ∈ I ^ d := by
  have := Ideal.mul_mem_mul (Ideal.pow_mem_pow ha (d - n)) hx
  rwa [← pow_add, Nat.sub_add_cancel hnd] at this

/-- If `ψ s = t * c`, `t ^ (m + N) * v = ψ (s ^ N * y)` and `d = m + N + e`, then
`ψ (s ^ (N + e) * y) = t ^ d * (c ^ e * v)`. -/
theorem map_pow_add_mul_eq_pow_mul {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {B : Type w} [CommRing B]
    (ψ : R →+* B) {s y : R} {t c v : B} {m N e d : ℕ} (hc : ψ s = t * c)
    (hv : t ^ (m + N) * v = ψ (s ^ N * y)) (hd : d = m + N + e) :
    ψ (s ^ (N + e) * y) = t ^ d * (c ^ e * v) := by
  have : ψ (s ^ (N + e) * y) = ψ s ^ e * ψ (s ^ N * y) := by
    rw [map_mul, map_mul, map_pow, map_pow, pow_add]
    ring
  rw [this, ← hv, hc, hd]
  ring

/-- **The numerators of the generators of the chart ideals generate a centre on the base.**

Let `I` be an ideal of `R`, let `a : ι → R` be a finite family of elements of `I`, and for each
`j` let `B j` be a ring under `R` — in the application, the affine blowup algebra `R[I/a j]` —
in which the extension of `I` is generated by the image of `a j` (`princ`). Let `K j` be an
ideal of `B j` generated by a finite family `z j : κ j → B j`, each member of which is a
fraction with numerator in a power of `I`: `φ j (a j) ^ n j l * z j l = φ j (x j l)` with
`x j l ∈ I ^ n j l` (`num`).

Assume the overlap condition `clear`: for every pair of charts `i`, `j` and every generator `l`
of `K i`, multiplying the fraction `x i l / a i ^ n i l` by a high enough power of `a i` makes
it a member of `K j`, in the denominator-free form
`φ j (a j) ^ (n i l + N) * v = φ j (a i ^ N * x i l)` for some `v ∈ K j`.

Then there are a `d > 0` and a finitely generated ideal `J ⊆ I ^ d` of `R` whose extension to
every chart is `(I · B j) ^ d · K j`.

`J` is generated by the elements `a i ^ (d - n i l) · x i l`, and `d` is one more than a common
bound for the sums `n i l + N`. -/
theorem exists_fg_le_pow_map_eq_pow_mul
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R) {ι : Type v} [Finite ι] (a : ι → R)
    (ha : ∀ i, a i ∈ I)
    {B : ι → Type w} [∀ j, CommRing (B j)] (φ : ∀ j, R →+* B j) (K : ∀ j, Ideal (B j))
    (princ : ∀ j, Ideal.map (φ j) I = Ideal.span {φ j (a j)})
    {κ : ι → Type*} [∀ j, Finite (κ j)] (z : ∀ j, κ j → B j)
    (hK : ∀ j, K j = Ideal.span (Set.range (z j)))
    (n : ∀ j, κ j → ℕ) (x : ∀ j, κ j → R)
    (hx : ∀ j l, x j l ∈ I ^ n j l)
    (num : ∀ j l, φ j (a j) ^ n j l * z j l = φ j (x j l))
    (clear : ∀ i j (l : κ i), ∃ (N : ℕ) (v : B j), v ∈ K j ∧
      φ j (a j) ^ (n i l + N) * v = φ j (a i ^ N * x i l)) :
    ∃ d : ℕ, 0 < d ∧ ∃ J : Ideal R, J.FG ∧ J ≤ I ^ d ∧
      ∀ j, Ideal.map (φ j) J = Ideal.map (φ j) I ^ d * K j := by
  classical
  have : Fintype ι := Fintype.ofFinite ι
  have : ∀ j, Fintype (κ j) := fun j ↦ Fintype.ofFinite (κ j)
  choose N v hv hNv using clear
  obtain ⟨d, hd0, hdN⟩ : ∃ d : ℕ, 0 < d ∧ ∀ i j l, n i l + N i j l ≤ d :=
    ⟨(Finset.univ.sup fun p : (Σ i, κ i) × ι ↦ n p.1.1 p.1.2 + N p.1.1 p.2 p.1.2) + 1,
      Nat.succ_pos _, fun i j l ↦ le_trans
        (Finset.le_sup (f := fun p : (Σ i, κ i) × ι ↦ n p.1.1 p.1.2 + N p.1.1 p.2 p.1.2)
          (Finset.mem_univ ((⟨i, l⟩ : Σ i, κ i), j))) (Nat.le_succ _)⟩
  have hdn : ∀ i (l : κ i), n i l ≤ d := fun i l ↦ (Nat.le_add_right _ _).trans (hdN i i l)
  have hdvd : ∀ j i, ∃ c : B j, φ j (a i) = φ j (a j) * c := by
    intro j i
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mp
      (((princ j) ▸ Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (φ j) (ha i) :
        φ j (a i) ∈ Ideal.span {φ j (a j)}))
    exact ⟨c, by rw [← hc, mul_comm]⟩
  choose c hc using hdvd
  refine ⟨d, hd0, Ideal.span
    (Set.range fun p : Σ i, κ i ↦ a p.1 ^ (d - n p.1 p.2) * x p.1 p.2),
    Submodule.fg_span (Set.finite_range _), ?_, fun j ↦ ?_⟩
  · refine Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_
    rintro _ ⟨⟨i, l⟩, rfl⟩
    exact pow_sub_mul_mem_pow (ha i) (hx i l) (hdn i l)
  rw [princ j]
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    refine Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_
    rintro _ ⟨⟨i, l⟩, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_add_of_le (hdN i j l)
    rw [SetLike.mem_coe, Ideal.mem_comap]
    change φ j (a i ^ (d - n i l) * x i l) ∈ Ideal.span {φ j (a j)} ^ d * K j
    rw [show d - n i l = N i j l + e by omega,
      map_pow_add_mul_eq_pow_mul (φ j) (hc j i) (hNv i j l) he]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_mul (Ideal.pow_mem_pow (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _) d)
      (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (hv i j l))
  · calc Ideal.span {φ j (a j)} ^ d * K j
        = Ideal.span {φ j (a j) ^ d} * Ideal.span (Set.range (z j)) := by
          rw [Ideal.span_singleton_pow, hK j]
      _ = Ideal.span ({φ j (a j) ^ d} * Set.range (z j)) := Ideal.span_mul_span _ _
      _ ≤ Ideal.map (φ j) _ := by
          refine Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_
          intro w hw
          obtain ⟨p, hp, q, hq, rfl⟩ := Set.mem_mul.mp hw
          obtain rfl : p = φ j (a j) ^ d := hp
          obtain ⟨l, rfl⟩ := hq
          have hcalc : φ j (a j) ^ d * z j l = φ j (a j ^ (d - n j l) * x j l) := by
            rw [map_mul, map_pow, ← num j l, ← mul_assoc, ← pow_add,
              Nat.sub_add_cancel (hdn j l)]
          rw [SetLike.mem_coe, hcalc]
          exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ (Ideal.subset_span ⟨(⟨j, l⟩ : Σ i, κ i), rfl⟩)

/-- **Clearing a denominator at a localization.** If the image of `w` in the localization of `B`
away from `u` lies in the extension of `K`, then some `u ^ N * w` already lies in `K`.

On the overlap of two charts of a blowup this is the passage from "the section lies in the ideal
sheaf over the overlap" to a statement on the chart itself: the overlap is the locus where the
transition element `u` is invertible. -/
theorem exists_pow_mul_mem_of_algebraMap_mem_map {B : Type u} [CommRing B] (K : Ideal B)
    (u w : B) {L : Type u} [CommRing L] [Algebra B L] [IsLocalization.Away u L]
    (h : algebraMap B L w ∈ K.map (algebraMap B L)) :
    ∃ N : ℕ, u ^ N * w ∈ K := by
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨N, rfl⟩, hm⟩ :=
    (IsLocalization.algebraMap_mem_map_algebraMap_iff (Submonoid.powers u) (S := L) K w).mp h
  exact ⟨N, hm⟩

/-- **The denominator-free form of the overlap condition.** Let `t` be the local generator of the
centre on the chart `B`, let `u` satisfy `t * u = ψ q` -- on a blowup chart `u` is the transition
element `q / t` -- and let `w = p / t ^ m` in the sense that `t ^ m * w = ψ p`. Then `u ^ N * w`
is `q ^ N * p` over `t ^ (m + N)`.

Together with `Stacks.Blowup.exists_pow_mul_mem_of_algebraMap_mem_map` this is exactly the
hypothesis `clear` of `Stacks.Blowup.exists_fg_le_pow_map_eq_pow_mul`. -/
theorem pow_mul_eq_map_of_pow_mul_eq {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {B : Type w} [CommRing B]
    (ψ : R →+* B) {t u : B} {p q : R} {m : ℕ} {w : B}
    (hu : t * u = ψ q) (hw : t ^ m * w = ψ p) (N : ℕ) :
    t ^ (m + N) * (u ^ N * w) = ψ (q ^ N * p) := by
  rw [map_mul, map_pow, ← hu, ← hw]
  ring

end Stacks.Blowup
